hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2007","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked, ""Who is most deserving of my good companionship and kind treatment?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Your mother."" He asked again, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Still your mother."" He asked a third time, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Still your mother."" He asked a fourth time, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then your father."
"2008","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The greatest of the major sins is that a man abuses his parents."" The people asked, ""How can a man abuse his own parents?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""A man abuses another man's father, and that man (in return) abuses his father... and he abuses another man's mother, and that man (in return) abuses his mother."
"2009","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “The one who severs the ties of kinship (i.e., breaks family relations) will not enter Paradise.”"
"2010","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (rahm) is derived from the Most Merciful (Rahman). (That is, the bond of kinship is connected and joined to Allah, the Most Merciful.) Therefore, Allah the Exalted said (regarding the bond of kinship): 'Whoever joins you, I will join him, and whoever severs you, I will sever him.'"
"2011","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say aloud, ""The children of such-and-such a person are not among my friends, and my friend is Allah and the righteous believers. But there is kinship with them. If they maintain it, I will maintain it; if they uphold the ties, I will uphold the ties."
"2012","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains ties of kinship is not the one who merely reciprocates (i.e., does good only in return for good), but the one who truly maintains ties of kinship is the one who joins relations when they have been severed."
"2013","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that a Bedouin came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said, ""You kiss children, but we do not kiss them."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""What can I do if Allah has not placed mercy in your heart (so how can I put it there now)?"
"2014","Narrated from Amir al-Mu’minin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that some captives were brought before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them was a woman whose breasts were full of milk, dripping, and whenever she found a child among the captives, she would take him to her belly and nurse him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: “Do you think this woman would throw her child into the fire?” We said: Never, as long as she is able, she would not throw her child into the fire. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah is more merciful to His servants than this woman is to her child.”"
"2015","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah divided mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Himself and sent down one part to the earth. Because of this one part, all creatures show mercy to one another, so much so that a mare lifts its hoof away from its young lest it should harm it."
"2016","‘Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said’ (When I was a child) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take hold of me and seat me on one thigh and Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) on the other thigh. Then he would embrace both of us and supplicate: “O Allah! Have mercy and kindness upon them, for I also show mercy to them.”"
"2017","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim who plants a tree and its fruit is eaten by people or animals, then for the one who planted it, there is the reward of charity (as if it is a continuous charity)."
"2018","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that` once the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to pray and we also stood up with him. Meanwhile, a Bedouin started supplicating during the prayer, saying: ""O Allah! Have mercy on me and on Muhammad (peace be upon him), and do not have mercy on anyone else."" When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished the prayer with salam, he said to the Bedouin: ""You have made something vast (i.e., Allah's mercy) restricted."
"2019","Narrated by Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will see the believers in their mutual mercy, love, and kindness like a single body; when one limb suffers, the whole body joins it in sleeplessness and fever."
"2020","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to others, (then from Allah) mercy will not be shown to him."
"2021","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gabriel (peace be upon him) emphasized to me so much about doing good to the neighbor that I thought he would make the neighbor an heir."
"2022","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""By Allah! He is not a believer, by Allah! He is not a believer, by Allah! He is not a believer."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who is that person?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""The one whose neighbor is not safe from his harm."
"2023","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Day of Resurrection should not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."
"2024","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The reward for telling a good word is equal to giving charity."
"2025","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in every matter.”"
"2026","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer to another believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."" And he interlaced his fingers to illustrate how they support each other. (Once it happened that) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting when a person, either a beggar or someone in need, came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards us and said: ""Intercede on behalf of this person, you will be rewarded, and Allah causes what He wills to be spoken by the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"2027","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not one who would speak abusively, utter obscenities, or curse others. When angry with any of us, he would say: ""What is the matter with him? May his forehead be covered with dust."
"2028","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): It never happened that anything was asked from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: ""No (I will not give it)."
"2029","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I served the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) for ten years. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) never even said ""Uff"" to me, nor ever said: ""Why did you do this?"" or ""Why did you not do this?"
"2030","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever calls a Muslim a sinner or a disbeliever, and in reality he is not a sinner or a disbeliever, then the one who said it will himself become a sinner and a disbeliever."
"2031","Narrated from Sayyiduna Thabit bin Dhahak (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by any religion other than Islam (i.e., deliberately swears to become a disbeliever), then he is as he has sworn (i.e., of that religion). And it is not obligatory upon the son of Adam to fulfill a vow which is beyond his capacity. And whoever commits suicide with anything in this world, he will be punished with that very thing on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever curses a believer, (its sin) is equal to killing him. And whoever calls a believer a disbeliever, this too is equal to killing him."
"2032","Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."
"2033","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a person was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man praised him greatly. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on you, you have cut his neck (by praising him like this)."" And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated this sentence several times. (Then he said): ""If any of you wants to praise someone unnecessarily, he should say: 'I think him to be such and such,' if he really believes him to be so, and Allah knows best about him (whether he is good or bad), and he should not say that he is good in the sight of Allah."
"2034","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not harbor malice and envy among yourselves, and do not cut off mutual relations, but be servants of Allah and brothers to each other. And it is not permissible for any Muslim to remain apart from his (Muslim) brother for more than three days due to any dispute."
"2035","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not search for (each other's) faults or investigate, and do not envy one another, nor turn away from one another, nor bear hatred against one another. Rather, be servants of Allah and brothers to one another."
"2036","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I think that so-and-so (those two persons) do not know anything about our religion."" And in another narration: ""I think that so-and-so people do not recognize our religion upon which we are."
"2037","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""All of my Ummah will be forgiven except those who commit sins openly. And the matter of openly committing is that a person does some sinful act at night, and in the morning, although Allah had concealed it, he goes around saying (to people), 'O so-and-so! I did such-and-such last night,' even though his Lord had concealed it for him at night, but in the morning he removes Allah's covering from himself."
"2038","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon meeting his (Muslim) brother for more than three nights (i.e.), when they meet, one turns his face away from the other and the other turns his face away from him, and the better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting and meeting."
"2039","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. And a person keeps speaking the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful person. And indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. And a person keeps telling lies until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."
"2040","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""No one is more patient over hearing something hurtful than Allah; people attribute a son to Allah, yet He forgives them and continues to provide for them."
"2041","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The strong man is not the one who defeats others in wrestling, but the strong man is the one who controls himself at the time of anger."
"2042","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to advise him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not get angry."" He asked several times (but) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not get angry."
"2043","Narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty brings nothing but good."
"2044","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “From the words that people have received from the previous prophets is this: If you do not feel shame, then do whatever you wish.”"
"2045","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to mix with us so much that I had a younger brother named Abu Umair. The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say to him: ""O Abu Umair! What happened to your little bird?"
"2046","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."" (After being bitten once, he remains cautious.)"
"2047","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some poetry is full of wisdom."
"2048","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the belly of any one of you were to be filled with pus, it would be better for him than to be filled with poetry."" (That is, if he remembers only poetry and nothing else, and especially those verses which are against the Shariah.)"
"2049","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that a desert dweller came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) be?"" (This hadith has previously appeared in the Book: The Virtues and Merits of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... Chapter: The Virtue of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)...), and here there is an addition that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will be with the one whom you love."" We asked, ""Will we also be (with you) in this way?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"2050","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, a flag will be set up for every treacherous person, and it will be announced: 'This is the treachery of so-and-so, the son of so-and-so.'"
"2051","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People say that 'Karam' is (the grapevine), whereas 'Karam' is the heart of a believer."
"2052","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): The name of Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) was previously ""Barrah"" (meaning pious and righteous). People said that she expresses her own purity, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named her Zainab."
"2053","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umm Sulaym was on a journey and the servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose name was Anjasha, was driving the camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Anjasha! Drive the glass vessels gently."" (By glass vessels, women are meant, i.e., ""O Anjasha! Drive the camels of these women gently."")"
"2054","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the worst name in the sight of Allah will be that of a person who is called Malik al-Amlak (i.e., King of Kings)."
"2055","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that two persons sneezed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied to one of them with ""Yarhamuk Allah"" (may Allah have mercy on you), but did not say anything to the other. It was asked of the Prophet (peace be upon him) why he said ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to one and not to the other. The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""He said 'Alhamdulillah' and the other did not say it."
"2056","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah likes sneezing and dislikes yawning. When someone sneezes and says 'Alhamdulillah', it becomes obligatory upon every Muslim who hears him to say 'Yarhamukallah'. But yawning is from Satan, so one should try to stop it as much as possible, because when a person yawns and says 'Ha', Satan laughs at him."
